                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is fun as hell, but also hard as hell. I've been playing for a while before it was on Steam, beta testing for the developer, and it's grown on me so much. Don't just get frustrated and walk away, for your own sake. It's a very punishing and difficult game, but so, so much fun when you find your groove.\n\nThere's a decent bit of enemy variety that ties itself together with level progression. Get further, get different, tougher, more varied enemies. The difficulty scales nicely, but it might feel like a brick wall until you get past the first hurdles. Fight through it. This isn't a game that holds your hand. \n\nThere are some little secrets and idiosyncrasies that are fun to discover. But mostly it's just fun, balls-to-the-wall action game, with the option to play more stealthfully if you'd like (and some nice point bonuses if you do).\n\nGive it a go. It's cheap, fun, and addicting.",
